From 26680b50f08fe5c5a063afa3b3dbdba291f1e224 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Krueckel <hi@felkru.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 02:22:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 33/54] Prompt Suggestions for a CLI coding agent in embedded
 builds

Embedded (remote_tty) builds have no Warp agent, so Prompt Suggestions now
ask the host app (window.warpPanelPromptSuggestion) with Warp's own request,
and accepting the chip starts the configured CLI coding agent in the
terminal with the prompt as its last argument (host.ai.prompt_suggestions_agent,
default "claude"). It's opt-in (host.ai.prompt_suggestions, off by default)
and only runs while private routing is on, since it sends the command and
its output. Warp's generic static prompts are skipped there.

Warp's in-band commands no longer cancel a pending suggestion: they start
right after each user command, so any host answer slower than a few hundred
milliseconds was dropped.

The "Prompt Suggestions" settings row becomes a real toggle plus the agent
command; the planned-feature placeholder widget is removed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
